&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is looking for a Senior Customer Trust Analyst to build and lead our customer-trust program across EMEA. As the first Customer Trust hire in the region, this person will partner closely with our EMEA-based Engineering and Sales teams to foster a culture of trust between Abnormal and our customers. This role sits within the Customer Trust team, which acts as the translation layer between customers and Abnormal: translating customer security requirements into internal controls, evidence, and product or operational requirements, then translating those controls back into clear assurances customers can trust and act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be responsible for presenting Abnormal&#39;s control environment directly to senior buyers, designing response strategy for the highest-stakes security reviews rather than reacting question by question, and driving toward clarity when customer expectations conflict with reality. This includes advising Sales leadership on how to position the control environment to prospects and defining how the trust response process scales as deal volume grows. As the first person in this function regionally, this individual will serve as the primary point of contact for Abnormal&#39;s EMEA customer-trust program and will be accountable for outcomes that unblock revenue at scale, not just individual deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate thrives in high-pressure customer conversations, translates security and privacy concepts for a business audience with precision, stays composed when a discussion turns contentious, and brings the business judgment to tie trust program depth to revenue outcomes. Familiarity with the EU AI Act and GDPR as they apply to a leading cybersecurity SaaS provider&#39;s customers is also expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience navigating customer-facing security conversations at the highest stakes level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical thinker who connects trust program depth to revenue outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in designing a response strategy rather than reacting question by question, even amid high ambiguity in the highest-stakes reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence and willingness to raise concerns and drive toward clarity when customer expectations conflict with reality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills with the ability to quickly build rapport with internal stakeholders and senior external buyers; demonstrated experience translating complex security and privacy concepts for diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and process, with the organizational rigor to be accountable for program-level outcomes, not just individual deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt to evolving business and technical environments and manage multiple priorities across deals in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player, collaborative work style&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and able to operate with minimal oversight, owning outcomes end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate as a self-starter and de facto leader, building a customer-trust function from the ground up as the first hire in a region, and comfortable navigating cross-functionally to manage customer requests without an established local team or playbook to lean on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and build the customer-trust program for EMEA as the first Customer Trust hire in the region, including how conversations are prioritized, escalated, and resolved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to defining how the trust response process scales as deal volume grows, without diluting response quality or turnaround time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer security requirements into internal controls, evidence, and product or operational requirements that internal teams can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and drive resolution of gaps between customer expectations and Abnormal&#39;s actual control environment, ensuring resolution is documented and communicated back to the customer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with EMEA-based Engineering and Sales teams, as well as Security and Legal, to foster a culture of trust between Abnormal and its customers across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor changes in customer expectations and the regulatory landscape, including the EU AI Act and GDPR, and adjust how Abnormal&#39;s control environment is presented as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain up-to-date content in Responsive and accurate documentation in Safebase Trust Center for EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the tooling that underpins the trust response process, including Responsive and Safebase Trust Center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage in ad-hoc projects as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain regular, clear communication with internal stakeholders and Sales leadership regarding conversation status, deal risk, and progress on unresolved issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate program status, health, and key risks to senior management and Sales leadership, connecting trust program performance to revenue outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must Haves&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 to 10 years of experience in customer-facing security, trust, or compliance roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, ISO 42001, RFPs, and security questionnaires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating customer security requirements into internal controls, evidence, and product or operational requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills with the ability to drive resolution across internal teams when customer expectations conflict with reality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain complex security and privacy concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping customers build trust with products in scope for the EU AI Act and GDPR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with German works councils&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CIPP/E, CIPM, CISM, CISSP, CTPRP, or ISO 27001 Lead Auditor certification(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Responsive and SafeBase Trust Center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-AA1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on AI in our process:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Abnormal AI uses AI-assisted tools to help our recruiting team prepare for candidate interviews. These tools analyze resume content and role requirements to suggest interview questions and areas for the interviewer to explore.They do not make hiring decisions or screen candidates automatically. Every decision about a candidacy is made by a person. Further, if your application is successful and Abnormal AI makes a conditional offer of employment, we will carry out pre-employment checks which must be successfully completed to progress to a final offer. All processes and pre-employment checks are in line with prevailing legislation and Abnormal AI&#39;s policies relevant to our security and privacy standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. For our EEO policy statement please &lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt9cbda641db7c0045/6a1e3d3a66aea075cd33e462/AAP_and_EEO_Statement.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;click here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. If you would like more information on your EEO rights under the law, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt4eb3a265cc7b1ca9/6a1e3d3bfe33e73c16ff026b/EEOC_Know_Your_Rights_Oct_30_2025.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR FUTURE, ON DEMAND&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal blend of stability and flexibility. A genuinely human employer that cares for people and the planet. True autonomy to shape what comes next, for us and you. This is the perfect platform to take your career where you want.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Back in 2005, we pioneered Europe’s first TV streaming service. Today, we&#39;re a leading TV streaming provider with millions of monthly users, and since 2021 we&#39;ve been ClimatePartner-certified. Over 200 colleagues of 47 nationalities. We’re the grown-up start-up, helping to shape a better future since day one.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;That hasn’t changed, even if the world has. We’re friendly, international, inclusive – and our people say we’re reliable and transparent, too. It’s why they trust us and believe in what we do.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Programmatic Sales GSA, you will be responsible for the automated and data-driven sale of our digital advertising inventory (primarily video and CTV) and report directly to the Director Sales All Markets. You will manage programmatic bookings, oversee the planning, implementation and optimisation of our initiatives to boost revenue in programmatic sales, and will therefore also be directly responsible for the optimisation and smooth, technical implementation of campaigns. This makes you the primary point of contact for agency trading desks in the GSA region regarding preferred deals and PMP strategies. You’ll also help with SSP and header bidding integrations and act as the link between Sales, Tech and AdOps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ADS TEAM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ads Team is a small but highly efficient team that combines technology and marketing to win customers over in the long term. With a presence in two countries (based in Berlin, Hamburg and Zurich) and operations in six countries, the Ads Team is a key driver of growth within Zattoo and has established itself as the market leader in CTV in Switzerland within a year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acquisition of new customers, advice, support and guide media agencies, trading desks and direct clients through our programmatic possibilities in a way they can understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drawing up and negotiating bespoke programme packages, private deals or preferred deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximise inventory revenue, skilfully manage floor prices (minimum prices) and analyse delivery rates and CPMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional sales teams in GSA to consult clients and pitch programmatic solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-lead the technical and commercial setup of Header Bidding and additional SSP integrations for CTV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-line technical ownership of programmatic delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical errors during delivery, analyse tracking issues and check campaign set-ups: troubleshoot deal delivery, floor pricing, and DSP configuration issues (e.g., SSAI, VAST responses, pod management, DSP/SSP bid stream mismatches).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain complex technical matters in simple terms to non-technical customers or internal departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in Programmatic Advertising, SSP Management, or Programmatic Account Management (strong experience in CTV/Video)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record in the sales of digital advertising products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of Google Ad Manager, DSP/SSP workflows, OpenRTB specs, and deal types (Preferred Deals, PMP, PG)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or strong technical familiarity with Header Bidding frameworks (e.g., Prebid) and SSP integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong network or understanding of the DACH Agency Trading Desk landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in German and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent, strong communicator, able to work under pressure, with strong negotiation skills&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teamplayer and creative thinker with a questioning mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHY JOIN US?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Zattoo, you’re always on firm ground with real freedom to explore. You’ll have the support and opportunity you need to go far, while you’re helping us create a sustainable and entertainment-filled future for all.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER YOU&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reward&lt;/strong&gt;: strong market competitive salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recharge&lt;/strong&gt;: 30 days vacation plus public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulate&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;trust based flexible working hours and the option for remote work worldwide for up to 8 weeks per year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;sharing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Free access to the best streaming experience on the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re developing: &lt;/strong&gt;Your own development budget, German classes and Zattoo all-company&amp;nbsp;hack days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re inclusive: ‘&lt;/strong&gt;Zattooies’ are a fun, engaged, and diverse team made up of 47 nationalities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re healthy:&lt;/strong&gt; Health checks, mental wellbeing support, team sports and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re responsible:&lt;/strong&gt; We are carbon neutral, an active employee Green team, discounted BVG tickets and free bike rentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re sociable: &lt;/strong&gt;A&amp;nbsp;calendar of events with fireside chats, lunches, in-house bar, BBQ’s, monthly socials, summer party and an annual off-site event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Zattoo enables our users to view indiscriminately and we reflect that in our team too. Regardless of race, gender, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, disability or any other characteristic protected by law we encourage everyone to apply and will give everyone equal consideration. We are an equal opportunities employer — join us and help build a diverse team dedicated to revolutionising the way you watch TV.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to ensuring fair, open, and equitable hiring practices and are happy to answer any questions you may have about us or the role throughout the whole process. In line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive, we share the applicable compensation range with you before your first interview.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-justify&quot;&gt;You can learn more about us at: &lt;a href=&quot;https://zattoo.com/company/jobs/&quot;&gt;https://zattoo.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;At Sony Music Entertainment, we fuel the creative journey. We’ve played a pioneering role in music history, from the first-ever music label to the invention of the flat disc record. We’ve nurtured some of music’s most iconic artists and produced some of the most influential recordings of all time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, we work in more than 70 countries, supporting a diverse roster of international superstars, developing and independent artists, and visionary creators. From our position at the intersection of music, entertainment, and technology, we bring imagination and expertise to the newest products and platforms, embrace new business models, employ breakthrough tools, and provide powerful insights that help our artists push creative boundaries and reach new audiences. In everything we do, we’re committed to artistic integrity, transparency, and entrepreneurship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Music Entertainment is a member of the Sony family of global companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Music’s Product, Design, Engineering &amp;amp; Global Operations (PDEGO) team is seeking a Lead Software Engineer within our Pub Admin product team in our King’s Cross office (London).&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;Pub Admin is our unified, modern rights and royalty platform - where our engineers help transform a complex domain into simple, scalable, high-performance product solutions for Sony Music’s global songwriting community.&lt;/p&gt;
